From: Pat Wendorf <dungeons@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] applet: wait longer for the panel connection

Upstream raised the daemon's wait for the panel from 1 s to 10 s in
epoch-1.11.0 (pop-os/cosmic-notifications#181). We used 30 s before that
fix, for a panel that is slow to start (cold start from a USB stick,
first-boot load): a panel that misses the handshake never starts its
applets -- an empty desktop with no panel or dock. Kept at 30 s until a
cold USB boot is proven on upstream's 10 s; then this patch is dropped.

Upstream: fixed with a shorter timeout in #181; not submitted
---
diff --git a/src/subscriptions/applet.rs b/src/subscriptions/applet.rs
index 56bd9bd..55d97ae 100644
--- a/src/subscriptions/applet.rs
+++ b/src/subscriptions/applet.rs
@@ -18,8 +18,11 @@ use std::os::unix::io::FromRawFd;
 pub async fn setup_panel_conn(tx: Sender<Input>) -> Result<Connection> {
     let socket = setup_panel_socket()?;
     let guid = Guid::generate();
+    // Wait for the panel as long as it may take to start: a panel slow to
+    // come up (cold start from USB, first-boot load) that misses the
+    // handshake never starts its applets. Upstream's 10 s is unproven there.
     let conn = tokio::time::timeout(
-        tokio::time::Duration::from_secs(10),
+        tokio::time::Duration::from_secs(30),
         Builder::socket(socket)
             .p2p()
             .server(guid)
